From fdc20857869a43e159882d9783020012d0eb07da Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <assistant@brenup.dev>
Date: Thu, 2 Jul 2026 10:39:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add text alignment controls to text blocks; vertical
 alignment for Image+Text
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Adds a Text alignment control (left/center/right) to every block with
primary heading/body text: HEADING, TEXT, QUOTE, CALLOUT, IMAGE_TEXT.
Adds a Vertical alignment control (top/middle/bottom) to IMAGE_TEXT's
text column only, since that's the one place a block currently has
extra vertical space to align within (next to the image) — other
blocks size exactly to their content, so a vertical control there
would sit in the UI and visibly do nothing.

Defaults preserve current rendering exactly for every existing block:
text_align defaults to left (matches the unset browser default),
vertical_align defaults to middle (matches the previously hardcoded
justify-center on IMAGE_TEXT's text column). No existing published
lesson changes appearance after this ships.

- app/admin/lessons/actions.ts: blockContentFromForm now records
  text_align (and vertical_align for IMAGE_TEXT) via two small
  sanitizing helpers that clamp to known values.
- components/LessonBuilderWorkspace.tsx: new reusable AlignmentGroup
  segmented control (radio buttons styled as icon buttons, submits
  natively via FormData, no client state needed), wired into the
  HEADING/TEXT/QUOTE/CALLOUT/IMAGE_TEXT editors.
- components/LessonBlockPreview.tsx: renders the stored alignment as
  explicit Tailwind classes at each text element (not relying on CSS
  inheritance from a parent, so alignment can't be silently
  overridden by another element's hardcoded class) for both the
  builder preview and the live student-facing lesson player, since
  both share this same renderer.

Verified with a full npm run build - compiles and type-checks clean,
zero new errors or warnings.
